From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Srirangan Madhavan <smadhavan@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:37:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: cxl: Do not reject committed zero-size HDM
 decoders

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2171032

Firmware may commit and lock unused HDM decoder slots with size 0 (CXL
r3.2 8.2.4.20.12), and "NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: cxl: Allow zero sized HDM
decoders" (591881a5890e) made init_hdm_decoder() return -ENOSPC for that
case so devm_cxl_enumerate_decoders() skips the empty slot and keeps
enumerating.

"NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: cxl: Share HDM decoder decode logic" (463d2a08ee53)
moved register decoding into cxl_hdm_decode_decoder() and added a
duplicate "enabled && !size" rejection there. That check runs first, so
init_hdm_decoder() returns -ENXIO before reaching its -ENOSPC skip and
endpoint enumeration aborts, silently defeating the merged feature.
cxl_pci_hdm_read_decoder() fails for the same reason, which independently
takes out the early PCI HDM cache used by CXL reset and vfio-cxl.

On NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72 with a 128 GiB CXL Type 3 device, decoder 1 is
committed and locked at size 0 (ctrl 0x1700), so the endpoint never probes:

  pci 0005:01:00.0: CXL HDM decoder 1 has invalid configuration: -6
  cxl_port endpoint9: decoder9.1: Invalid decoder configuration (ctrl: 0x1700): -6
  cxl_port endpoint9: Failed to initialize decoder9.1
  cxl_mem mem0: endpoint9 failed probe

The device stays in the "disabled" state, no region is assembled, and the
128 GiB range is absent from lsmem and from its NUMA node.

Keep caller-owned policy out of the decode helper so a committed
zero-size decoder decodes successfully as an empty HPA range, letting the
existing init_hdm_decoder() rejection do the skipping. Skip empty ranges
when collecting CXL reset windows, since they map no HPA and would
otherwise be rejected by cxl_hdm_range_add() as end < start, or by
cxl_hdm_range_len() as an overflow when base is 0.

Both hunks are required together: dropping the shared check alone makes
cxl_pci_hdm_read_decoder() accept the slot and hand an empty range to the
reset path.

Upstream folded these two hunks into the series from v11 onwards rather
than adding a separate patch, so this backport takes them from the
corresponding patches of the posted series instead of adding a fixup.

Fixes: 463d2a08ee53 ("NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: cxl: Share HDM decoder decode logic")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-cxl/20261011021422.3428136-8-smadhavan@nvidia.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-cxl/20261011021422.3428136-12-smadhavan@nvidia.com/
Reported-by: Fenghua Yu <fenghuay@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Srirangan Madhavan <smadhavan@nvidia.com>
(backported from https://lore.kernel.org/linux-cxl/20261011021422.3428136-1-smadhavan@nvidia.com/)
Signed-off-by: Jiandi An <jan@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Matthew R. Ochs <mochs@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-02231
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@12bc47fb5529e04e8af226c7d37ee22c8c907950
---
 drivers/cxl/core/reset.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cxl/core/reset.c b/drivers/cxl/core/reset.c
index 1caf2afdcd90..f4ac72c34b69 100644
--- a/drivers/cxl/core/reset.c
+++ b/drivers/cxl/core/reset.c
@@ -168,8 +168,6 @@ int cxl_hdm_decode_decoder(struct cxl_decoder_settings *settings, int id,
 	if (base == U64_MAX || size == U64_MAX ||
 	    (size && base > U64_MAX - (size - 1)))
 		return -ENXIO;
-	if (enabled && !size)
-		return -ENXIO;
 
 	settings->hpa_range = (struct range) {
 		.start = base,
@@ -1048,6 +1046,10 @@ static int cxl_hdm_ranges_collect(struct cxl_hdm_range_context *ctx,
 		if (!(settings->flags & CXL_DECODER_F_ENABLE))
 			continue;
 
+		/* A committed zero-size decoder maps no HPA. */
+		if (!range_len(&settings->hpa_range))
+			continue;
+
 		if (settings->flags & CXL_DECODER_F_NORMALIZED_ADDRESSING) {
 			pci_err(pdev,
 				"CXL reset does not support normalized address decoders\n");
